# candy-ui — Adding New Components

## 0. Project overview

Published npm package **`@dalshenekuda/candy-ui`**: React 18+ UI kit for storefront apps (Hydrogen and any React stack).

- **Stack:** React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + Radix UI (Dialog, Aside, Slot on Button) + CVA + `cn()` (clsx + tailwind-merge).
- **Typography scale:** SCSS generates `.typo-*` classes (responsive at 992px); prefer `<Text>` or existing `.typo-*` in components — do not add raw `font-size` in TSX.

### File structure

```
src/
├── index.ts                  library entry; side-effect CSS + named exports
├── main.ts                   dev-only app entry
├── lib/utils.ts              cn() helper
├── tokens/                   CSS tokens (colors, spacing, typography SCSS)
├── components/<Name>/        <Name>.tsx + <Name>.stories.ts(x)
└── styles/                   style.css → imported by index.ts
```

## 1. Where to place a component

| Type | Location |
|------|----------|
| Any library component | `src/components/<Name>/` — TSX + CVA + Tailwind |

Do not add `src/primitives/`, `domain-level/`, per-component `index.ts`, or Vue-style `install()` registration.

## 2. Component folder structure

```
src/components/<ComponentName>/
  <ComponentName>.tsx           ← component + types inline
  <ComponentName>.stories.ts    ← Storybook (or .tsx if JSX in stories)
```

- Types live **inline** in the `.tsx` file unless types must be exported for consumers.
- Always use `@/` alias: `import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'`.
- Use `cn()` for all className composition.
- Use `cva` from `class-variance-authority` for variant logic.

### CVA pattern

```tsx
import { cva, type VariantProps } from 'class-variance-authority'
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'

const componentVariants = cva('base-classes', {
  variants: {
    variant: {
      default: 'bg-brand text-text-on-brand hover:bg-brand-hover',
      outline: 'border border-border bg-surface hover:bg-surface-raised text-text',
      ghost: 'hover:bg-surface-raised text-text-muted',
      danger: 'bg-danger text-text-on-brand hover:opacity-90',
    },
    size: {
      sm: 'h-8 px-sm',
      md: 'h-10 px-md',
      lg: 'h-12 px-lg',
    },
  },
  defaultVariants: { variant: 'default', size: 'md' },
})

interface ComponentProps
  extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLElement>,
    VariantProps<typeof componentVariants> {}
```

### shadcn → our tokens mapping (MANDATORY — never use shadcn defaults)

| shadcn class | our class |
|---|---|
| `bg-primary` | `bg-brand` |
| `text-primary-foreground` | `text-text-on-brand` |
| `bg-destructive` | `bg-danger` |
| `bg-background` | `bg-surface` |
| `bg-secondary` | `bg-surface-raised` |
| `text-foreground` | `text-text` |
| `text-muted-foreground` | `text-text-muted` |
| `bg-accent` (hover) | `bg-surface-raised` |
| `text-primary` (link) | `text-brand` |
| `border-input` | `border-border` |
| `ring-ring` | `ring-brand` |
| `fill-muted-foreground` | `fill-text-muted` |
| `fill-muted` | `fill-surface` |

## 3. Styling — NEVER use Bootstrap or hardcoded values

**No Bootstrap classes** (`d-flex`, `col-*`, `px-3`, `mb-2`, etc.) — use Tailwind utilities instead.

**No new custom `@media` queries** in component SCSS — use Tailwind breakpoints from `tailwind.preset.js` (e.g. `desktop:`).

- **Mobile first:** default styles up to `991px`.
- **Desktop:** from `992px`, use the `desktop:` prefix (e.g. `desktop:flex-row`).

| What | Do | Never |
|------|----|-------|
| Colors | `var(--color-text)` or Tailwind `text-text`, `bg-brand` | raw hex or Bootstrap `text-primary` |
| Spacing | `var(--spacing-md)` or Tailwind `p-md`, `gap-sm` | `16px` or Bootstrap `p-3` |
| Font size | `<Text variant="body-md">` or class `typo-body-md` | `font-size: 16px` in component CSS |
| Font weight | `weight` on Text or `font-semibold` | hardcoded `font-weight: 600` |
| Border radius | `rounded-md` / `var(--radius-md)` | `12px` |
| Transitions | `duration-base` / `var(--transition-base)` | `200ms` |
| Breakpoints | `desktop:block` | new `@media (min-width: 992px)` in components |

Tailwind is for **layout** (`flex`, `gap-sm`, `px-md`, `items-center`).

## 4. Token flow — single source of truth

```
src/tokens/colors/palette.css           ← hex ONLY (--palette-*)
src/tokens/colors/theme-light.css       ← semantic (--color-*) light
src/tokens/colors/theme-dark.css        ← semantic dark (.dark on <html>)
src/tokens/colors/tones.css             ← flavor tones (data-tone / data-tone-vars)
src/tokens/spacing/spacing.css          ← --spacing-*
src/tokens/base.css                     ← radius, shadows, transitions
src/tokens/typography/*.scss            ← font scale → .typo-* classes
src/styles/style.css                    ← imports tokens + @tailwind
tailwind.preset.js                      ← maps CSS vars to Tailwind theme (consumers)
```

Do not add hex to TS token files for runtime colors. Do not reference removed paths like `src/ui/tokens/` or `design-tokens.ts`.

**Dark theme:** consumers toggle `class="dark"` on `<html>` (`darkMode: 'class'` in preset).

## 5. API design (React)

- Use standard React patterns: `open` / `onOpenChange` for Radix roots where applicable, or uncontrolled Radix defaults.
- Do not use Vue names (`modelValue`, `update:modelValue`, emits, slots in docs).

## 6. Text component API

```tsx
<Text variant="body-md" weight="semibold" color="color-text" as="span">
  Label
</Text>
```

- `variant` → `display-2xl` … `overline` (see `src/components/Text/Text.tsx`)
- `color` → semantic token **name without `--`**: `color-text`, `color-text-muted`, `color-brand`, `tone-ink`, etc.
- `weight` → `light` | `regular` | `medium` | `semibold` | `bold` | `black`
- `as` → override HTML tag; `balance` → `text-balance` on display headings

Use `<Text>` for visible copy in components. Avoid raw `<span>` / `<p>` with inline font sizes.

## 7. Surfaces and commerce helpers

- **Card:** use `Card`, `CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, `CardDescription`, `CardContent`, `CardFooter` — not a separate ContentPlate primitive.
- **ProductCard:** `price` / `compareAtPrice` are **`ReactNode`** (app formats money); do not assume cents inside the kit.
- Do not add component aliases in `src/index.ts`.

## 8. Exports — mandatory after adding a component

1. Add a named re-export in `src/index.ts`:

```ts
export * from './components/MyComponent/MyComponent';
```

2. Do **not** register via `app.component()` or a plugin `install()`.

**`tsconfig.build.json`** must keep `"paths": { "@/*": ["src/*"] }` for alias resolution in declarations.

## 9. Stories structure and documentation

Every component MUST document behavior in `.stories.ts` / `.stories.tsx`:

1. **`parameters.docs.description.component`** — purpose and responsive behavior.
2. **`argTypes`** — props with `table.category`: `'Data' | 'Appearance' | 'State'` (and `'Slots'` for `ReactNode` props like `footer`).
3. Use **`Meta` / `StoryObj` from `@storybook/react`**, title prefix **`Components/<Name>`** (or `Tokens/…` for token stories).

```ts
const meta: Meta<typeof MyComponent> = {
  title: 'Components/MyComponent',
  component: MyComponent,
  tags: ['autodocs'],
  parameters: {
    docs: {
      description: { component: 'What it does and how it behaves on mobile vs desktop.' },
    },
  },
  argTypes: {
    disabled: {
      description: 'Disables interaction.',
      table: { category: 'State' },
    },
    footer: {
      description: 'Optional footer slot content.',
      table: { category: 'Slots', type: { summary: 'ReactNode' } },
      control: false,
    },
  },
};
```

- One named export per meaningful state (e.g. `OnSale`, `Loading`).
- Mock data in named constants at the top of the file when needed.

## 10. What NOT to do

- ALL code comments MUST be in English
- Do not hardcode hex colors, px sizes, or ms durations in component styles
- Do not use Bootstrap anywhere
- Do not add `reka-ui` — Radix packages used directly are bundled dependencies
- Do not use legacy typography variants (`h1`, `b2`, `primary-color-1`)
- Do not document or implement Vue SFC / `<script setup>` patterns in this repo
